  "findings": [
    "B readiness median/max decreased from 103.984/242.521ms to 27.9825/108.346ms in the retained exact-build successful pairs.",
    "B native remaining pair readiness median/max decreased from 77.994/120.322ms to 10.2955/11.990ms. All 12 sampled entries used prepared candidates; no expired fallback was observed.",
    "Only one successful pair has a measured builder join, equal to zero. The other 11 joins are unmeasured, not measured zero.",
    "B first input dispatch median/max decreased; worst-dispatch median increased from 3.262 to 4.698ms while its sampled maximum decreased from 24.108 to 8.792ms. These runs do not prove that spare construction has no active-input cost.",
    "A capture activation median/max increased from 12.315/46.760ms to 23.4265/367.510ms. Overall stutter is not resolved.",
    "The worst A activation spends 345.372ms in local worker IPC response wait and 22.137ms in IPC authority; exact worker subphase costs are not available. Native foreground bucket is under 10ms and native total bucket is 10-100ms, so do not attribute the entire IPC wait to foreground calls.",
    "The same crossing has 106 sampled TCP retransmitted bytes and 221.840ms exchange residual; transport/endpoint delay and local activation delay are separate measurements, and one does not prove the cause of the other.",
    "The largest B readiness sample has only 11.990ms native pair remaining time; its longer service-local admission/authentication/receive waits are separate from native readiness and can overlap broader spans.",
    "No matching-build failure events or new recovery failures were found in retained logs; both input services remain READY."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Software spans are not cursor-visible end-to-end latency. Different trajectories, intervals and sample counts do not isolate the patch as the sole cause.",
    "All 12 detailed retained pairs lie in the fast burst ending around 13:16:39 UTC (A clock). Subsequent coarse input events exist, but the collector retains at most 12 attempts per 120-second window. The later requested 3-5 second dwell cases cannot be separately quantified from these profiles.",
    "Native activation stages and worker stages are timing buckets, not exact durations. The worker IPC response includes work not fully covered by native activation timing.",
    "Exchange residual includes transport and endpoint scheduling/read loops, not pure network RTT. Never subtract B ReadyWait from source grant wait to name the difference network latency.",
    "Input dispatch maxima describe retained per-attempt records, not a percentile across every physical input event.",
    "TCP counter snapshots are per-attempt deltas; their sampled sum does not establish complete connection traffic totals.",
    "Empty incomplete rotated control logs do not establish complete UI history."
  ],
